codex
The residual also exposes the real blocker in the index-based design: `intSeqAt` is intentionally partial in the reference semantics, and length bounds do not let the backend prove definedness for an opaque symbolic sequence. I’m redesigning the implementation to iterate over the string structurally and retain the previous two character codes. That keeps all executed values defined and gives a structurally recursive, exact loop summary—no totalized selector or execution bridge is needed.
